-- CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2 (2026-10-19, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 2826 PATHS-UNTESTED-1 and 2880 controls_on_critical_path_untested). Second seed of the table
-- migrations/2026-10-19-control-alternate-probes.sql creates (applied first: this name sorts after it). That file seeded 23 probes from a read of 13:00Z (control_registry
-- 75 rows). At 14:5xZ the register held 91 rows: sixteen controls were registered in between, eleven of them without an alternate tested date, four on the critical
-- path (claim-integrity-gate, research-floor-extend, research-revise-shrink-guard, research-width-governor), so the detector fm-control-alternate-undrilled would have read
-- 11 at birth and controls_on_critical_path_untested reads 4 again. This file gives the eight whose alternate a D1 read can observe their read-only expected/observed
-- probe, in the shape of the first file (state of the lever and the backup objects, plus an event inside a window; nothing is stamped from a declaration), and the probe
-- of the parked loop-owned contract control that LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1 registers (a probe row may exist before its control row: the views join from
-- control_registry). Three registered controls stay without a probe on purpose: model_floor_pr_check (the alternate is a CI workflow), research-model-skip-gauge (an
-- isolate's memory) and research-fallback-price-guard (a rate constant in code) have no trace in D1, and a decorative probe would stamp a declaration. The detector reads
-- 3 after this file; each is closed by an exerciser that lives where the alternate lives, or by a recorded ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE reason.
-- Live read-only runs 2026-10-19 14:5xZ: the eight probes of controls that already exist return ok against qnfo-audit (ops_config keys that are absent read as their default, as the
-- workers read them); the ninth reads the objects LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1 creates and returned 'the red-drain park step ... is missing' until that file is applied.
-- Rows written: control_alternate_probes 9 (INSERT OR IGNORE, none exist yet), control_registry evidence on the controls that exist (at most 8, a NOT LIKE guard makes a second
-- apply change nothing), decision_log 1. No DELETE, no DROP.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = replace(evidence, ' | CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2 2026-10-19: probed by its control_alternate_probes row (second seed, controls registered after CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-1), which the chaos drill runs once CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-RUNNER-1 lands, and only a passing probe stamps alternate_tested_at', '') WHERE evidence LIKE '%CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2 2026-10-19%'; DELETE FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control IN ('claim-integrity-gate', 'research-floor-extend', 'research-revise-shrink-guard', 'research-width-governor', 'code_reasoning_low', 'loop_breaker_tool_exclusions', 'research-floor-rearm', 'research-kimi-last-resort', 'loop-owned-contract-park')
-- Rollback note: the decision_log row stays (append-only).

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_alternate_probes (control, probe_sql, window_note, enabled) VALUES
 ('claim-integrity-gate',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''table'' AND name = ''paper_integrity_backups'') THEN ''the backup table paper_integrity_backups is missing, so a corrected paper could not be restored'' WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''claim_integrity_mode''), ''enforce'') NOT IN (''enforce'', ''measure'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config claim_integrity_mode holds a value the gate does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind IN (''claim-gate'', ''claim-integrity'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-48 hours'')) THEN ''no claim-gate or claim-integrity event in 48 h, so the gate and its sweep are not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '48 h: the held-paper gate and its sweep log an event every research cycle; the backup table is what the correction path restores from; the sentences the gate holds are pinned by qnfo-research-exec/claim-integrity.test.mjs', 1),
 ('research-floor-extend',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_floor_extend''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'', ''enforce'', ''measure'') THEN ''ops_config research_floor_extend holds a value the stage does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind IN (''floor-extend'', ''floor-route'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-48 hours'')) THEN ''no floor-extend or floor-route event in 48 h, so the extension route is not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '48 h: the extension route logs floor-extend and floor-route events (15 and 5 in 6 hours on 2026-10-19); the absent key reads as on', 1),
 ('research-revise-shrink-guard',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_revise_shrink_guard''), ''enforce'') NOT IN (''enforce'', ''measure'', ''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard holds a value the stage does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind IN (''revise-patch'') AND status IN (''ok'', ''warn'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-48 hours'')) THEN ''the revise route recorded no revise-patch event in 48 h, so the guard has no path to protect'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '48 h: every patch the reviser applies logs revise-patch (1670 in 24 h on 2026-10-19); the refusal itself (revise-shrink-refused) is event-driven and is pinned by the stage test; the absent key reads as enforce', 1),
 ('research-width-governor',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_governor''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_governor holds a value the governor does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind IN (''research-width'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-48 hours'')) THEN ''no research-width event in 48 h, so the governor is not adjusting the width'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '48 h: the governor logs research-width on each change of the cap (5 in 24 h on 2026-10-19); the absent key reads as on', 1),
 ('code_reasoning_low',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN trim(COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_reasoning_low''), ''on'')) = '''' THEN ''ops_config code_reasoning_low is blank, so the off lever reads as on by accident'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM code_tasks WHERE status IN (''merged'', ''failed'', ''needs_human'', ''superseded'', ''closed'') AND updated_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ'', ''now'', ''-24 hours'')) THEN ''no code task reached a terminal status in 24 h, so the model ladder that carries the option has not run'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '24 h: the ladder runs on every code task; the rejection fallback and the off switch are pinned by qnfo-code-orchestrator/reasoning-low.test.mjs; the key is absent while the option is on', 1),
 ('loop_breaker_tool_exclusions',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''view'' AND name = ''tool_failures_excluded_24h'') THEN ''the view tool_failures_excluded_24h is missing, so excluded errors are no longer listed'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''view'' AND name = ''v_loop_breaker_signatures'' AND sql LIKE ''%tool_error_exclusions%'') THEN ''v_loop_breaker_signatures no longer reads tool_error_exclusions'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions WHERE rationale IS NULL OR trim(rationale) = '''') THEN ''an exclusion pattern has no rationale'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe: every excluded error stays listed and every pattern keeps its rationale; the loop breaker view still reads the exclusion table', 1),
 ('research-floor-rearm',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''park_rearm''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config park_rearm holds a value the sweep does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''table'' AND name = ''bak_20261019_research_parked'') THEN ''the backup table bak_20261019_research_parked is missing, so the rollback line has nothing to restore'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind IN (''park-rearm-tick'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-48 hours'')) THEN ''no park-rearm-tick event in 48 h, so the hourly sweep is not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '48 h: the sweep logs park-rearm-tick every hour (6 in 6 hours on 2026-10-19); the absent key reads as on', 1),
 ('research-kimi-last-resort',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_kimi_last_resort''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_kimi_last_resort holds a value the chain does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind IN (''revise-patch'') AND status IN (''ok'', ''warn'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-48 hours'')) THEN ''the revise route recorded no revise-patch event in 48 h, so the model chain the last resort belongs to has not run'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '48 h: state probe on the lever and on the route the chain serves; the chain order and the off switch are pinned by the research-exec suites', 1),
 ('loop-owned-contract-park',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM fleet_tasks WHERE id = ''red-drain'' AND instr(definition, ''LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1'') > 0) THEN ''the red-drain park step LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1 is missing, so a circular loop-owned contract that is active again is not re-parked'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''trigger'' AND name = ''contract_probe_templates_loop_merged'' AND instr(sql, ''LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1'') > 0) THEN ''the birth trigger no longer parks a loop-owned contract'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = ''fm-loop-owned-contract-circular'' AND status = ''active'') THEN ''the detector fm-loop-owned-contract-circular is missing or not active'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = c.issue_id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND c.status IN (''active'', ''holding'') AND instr(c.verify_probe, ''SELECT status FROM agent_issues WHERE id ='') > 0) THEN ''a circular loop-owned contract of an open issue is active again'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe: the birth trigger and the hourly red-drain step are the two producers of the parked state, the detector is the third reader; the control row comes from LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1 (this probe row may exist before that control row does)', 1);

UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = evidence || ' | CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2 2026-10-19: probed by its control_alternate_probes row (second seed, controls registered after CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-1), which the chaos drill runs once CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-RUNNER-1 lands, and only a passing probe stamps alternate_tested_at'
WHERE control IN ('claim-integrity-gate', 'research-floor-extend', 'research-revise-shrink-guard', 'research-width-governor', 'code_reasoning_low', 'loop_breaker_tool_exclusions', 'research-floor-rearm', 'research-kimi-last-resort', 'loop-owned-contract-park') AND evidence NOT LIKE '%CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2 2026-10-19%' AND evidence NOT LIKE '%CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-1 2026-10-19%';

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session_01JADz8uHqYt9eUMBTwbbBE6',
  'a control alternate counts as tested only while a probe on its own evidence keeps passing, and the first seed of control_alternate_probes was taken from a register that has since grown, so the probes of the controls registered after it are added where a D1 read can observe their alternate and are not invented where it cannot',
  'CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2: nine read-only expected/observed probes in control_alternate_probes (claim-integrity-gate, research-floor-extend, research-revise-shrink-guard, research-width-governor, code_reasoning_low, loop_breaker_tool_exclusions, research-floor-rearm, research-kimi-last-resort, loop-owned-contract-park); model_floor_pr_check, research-model-skip-gauge and research-fallback-price-guard are left unprobed because their alternates leave no trace in D1',
  'qnfo-audit 2026-10-19 14:5xZ (SELECT only): control_registry 91 rows, 29 alternate-untested, scorecard controls_on_critical_path_untested 4 (the four critical controls above); ops_config keys claim_integrity_mode enforce, research_governor on, research_kimi_last_resort on, the other levers absent (default on); events claim-gate 31, floor-extend 15, park-rearm-tick 6, research-width 5 in the last 6 to 24 hours; tables paper_integrity_backups and bak_20261019_research_parked and the views tool_failures_excluded_24h and v_loop_breaker_signatures exist; eight probes were run read-only and returned ok, the ninth correctly reported that the park step of LOOP-OWNED-CONTRACT-MONITORING-1 does not exist yet',
  'migration merged',
  'nine control_alternate_probes rows and an evidence note on at most eight control_registry rows; nothing runs the probes until CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-RUNNER-1 lands, so no control is stamped tested by this file',
  'the Rollback header of migrations/2026-10-19-control-alternate-probes2.sql',
  'every control whose alternate a D1 read can observe has a probe a runner or a session can execute',
  'controls_on_critical_path_untested <= 4 within 6 h',
  'none',
  'd1:qnfo-audit read-only probe runs, node:sqlite fixtures in migrations/control-alternate-probes2.test.mjs'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE action LIKE 'CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-2:%');
